  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MIFSSA II (AC)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Weiterentwicklung der Mikrofinanzinitiative f&#xfc;r Sub-Sahara Afrika (MIFSSA II)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Ausweitung der Mikr</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ShoreCap III was established in 2017 and focuses on providing equity and capacity building to various African financial institutions, including small business banks, microfinance institutions, insurance companies, leasing companies, housing finance companies and fintech providers. The fund invests in equity, quasi-equity, shareholder loans and convertible debt. It focuses on competitive returns for investors and provides final beneficiaries with access to scarce equity, governance support, environmental, social and governance (ESG) compliance and strategic advice through capacity building initiatives. In addition, the Fund emphasises compliance with environmental and social standards in accordance with recognised guidelines.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ShoreCap III was established in 2017 and focuses on providing equity and capacity building to various African financial institutions, including small business banks, microfinance institutions, insurance companies, leasing companies, housing finance companies and fintech providers. The fund invests in equity, quasi-equity, shareholder loans and convertible debt. It focuses on competitive returns for investors and provides final beneficiaries with access to scarce equity, governance support, environmental, social and governance (ESG) compliance and strategic advice through capacity building initiatives. In addition, the Fund emphasises compliance with environmental and social standards in accordance with recognised guidelines.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="DE">ShoreCap III wurde 2017 gegr&#xfc;ndet und konzentriert sich auf die Bereitstellung von Eigenkapital und den Aufbau von Kapazit&#xe4;ten f&#xfc;r verschiedene afrikanische Finanzinstitutionen, darunter Banken f&#xfc;r kleine Unternehmen, Mikrofinanzinstitutionen, Versicherungen, Leasingunternehmen, Wohnungsbaufinanzierungsgesellschaften und Fintech-Anbieter. Der Fondsinvestiert in Eigenkapital, Quasi-Eigenkapital, Gesellschafterdarlehen und Wandelanleihen. Dabei legt er den Schwerpunkt auf wettbewerbsf&#xe4;hige Renditen f&#xfc;r die Anleger und bietet den Endbeg&#xfc;nstigten Zugang zu knappem Eigenkapital, Unterst&#xfc;tzung bei Unternehmensf&#xfc;hrung, der Einhaltung von Umwelt-, Sozial- und Unternehmensf&#xfc;hrungsstandards (ESG) sowie strategische Beratung durch Initiativen zum Kapazit&#xe4;tsaufbau. Dar&#xfc;ber hinaus legt der Fonds Wert auf die Einhaltung von Umwelt- und Sozialstandards gem&#xe4;&#xdf; anerkannten Richtlinien.</narrative>
  </description>
